        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "*Structure — Desktop*\n\n1. Given a shopper visits a page where the Disclaimer is configured to appear, when the page loads, then the Disclaimer component renders above the Footer with a left-aligned title, body text paragraph, and READ MORE link, consistent with the Figma design.\n2. Given a shopper views the Disclaimer on desktop, when it renders, then the title is displayed on the left and the body text and READ MORE link are displayed on the right, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Structure — Tablet*\n\n3. Given a shopper visits a page on tablet where the Disclaimer is configured to appear, when the page loads, then the Disclaimer component renders consistently with desktop, sized appropriately for the tablet viewport, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Structure — Mobile*\n\n4. Given a shopper visits a page on mobile where the Disclaimer is configured to appear, when the page loads, then the Disclaimer component renders with the title stacked above the body text and READ MORE link, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Content — Contentful Driven*\n\n5. Given the Disclaimer component renders, when it fetches content from Contentful, then the title, body text, and READ MORE link label and destination are all driven by Contentful and are not hardcoded in the component.\n6. Given the Disclaimer component renders on a specific storefront, when it fetches content, then it reads from the correct Contentful locale for that storefront ensuring regional variations are reflected correctly.\n7. Given Contentful content has not been authored or a fetch fails, when the Disclaimer component attempts to render, then the component does not render and the page remains unaffected, consistent with the global fallback pattern.\n\n*READ MORE Link*\n\n8. Given a shopper clicks the READ MORE link, when the interaction occurs, then they are navigated to a page on the storefront. Note: confirm with Zimmermann which page the READ MORE link should navigate to — to be finalised before build.\n\n*Page Visibility*\n\n9. Given the Disclaimer component is configured to appear on specific pages only, when a shopper visits a page where it is not configured, then the component does not render and the page layout is unaffected.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n10. Given a keyboard-only user navigates to the Disclaimer, when they Tab to the READ MORE link, then it receives focus and is reachable without a mouse.\n11. Given a screen reader user navigates to the Disclaimer, when it renders, then the title, body text, and READ MORE link are all announced correctly.",
            "to_string": "*Structure — Desktop*\n\n1. Given a shopper visits a page where the Disclaimer is configured to appear, when the page loads, then the Disclaimer component renders above the Footer with a left-aligned title, body text paragraph, and READ MORE link, consistent with the Figma design.\n2. Given a shopper views the Disclaimer on desktop, when it renders, then the title is displayed on the left and the body text and READ MORE link are displayed on the right, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Structure — Tablet*\n\n3. Given a shopper visits a page on tablet where the Disclaimer is configured to appear, when the page loads, then the Disclaimer component renders consistently with desktop, sized appropriately for the tablet viewport, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Structure — Mobile*\n\n4. Given a shopper visits a page on mobile where the Disclaimer is configured to appear, when the page loads, then the Disclaimer component renders with the title stacked above the body text and READ MORE link, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Content — Contentful Driven*\n\n5. Given the Disclaimer component renders, when it fetches content from Contentful, then the title, body text, and READ MORE link label and destination are all driven by Contentful and are not hardcoded in the component.\n6. Given the Disclaimer component renders on a specific storefront, when it fetches content, then it reads from the correct Contentful locale for that storefront ensuring regional variations are reflected correctly.\n7. Given Contentful content has not been authored or a fetch fails, when the Disclaimer component attempts to render, then the component does not render and the page remains unaffected, consistent with the global fallback pattern.\n\n*READ MORE Link*\n\n{color:#ff5630}8. Given a shopper clicks the READ MORE link, when the interaction occurs, then they are navigated to a page on the storefront. Note: confirm with Zimmermann which page the READ MORE link should navigate to — to be finalised before build.{color}\n\n*Page Visibility*\n\n9. Given the Disclaimer component is configured to appear on specific pages only, when a shopper visits a page where it is not configured, then the component does not render and the page layout is unaffected.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n10. Given a keyboard-only user navigates to the Disclaimer, when they Tab to the READ MORE link, then it receives focus and is reachable without a mouse.\n11. Given a screen reader user navigates to the Disclaimer, when it renders, then the title, body text, and READ MORE link are all announced correctly.",
