      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Developer, \nI want a reusable {{global/country-currency-selector}} React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \nso that it can be consumed across storefronts to allow shoppers to select their shipping country, currency, and optionally language.\n\n----\n\nThe component is a right-anchored slide-in drawer. It accepts props to control which optional sections render. It does not own redirect logic — it exposes an {{onConfirm(country, locale)}} callback; the consuming page handles the redirect.\n\nFigma: {{QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs}}, nodes {{3193:72555}} (desktop), {{3193:72676}} (desktop with language), {{3193:73142}} (mobile), {{3193:73415}} (mobile with language). UI kit: {{wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm}}, node {{40000938-5082}}.\n\n----\n\n\n\n----\n\n*Dependencies*\n\n* Depends on SFCC-44 (country-to-storefront routing and country-currency mapping) — the component consumes this config to build the country list and determine currency codes per country.\n* Depends on SFCC-688 (functional story) for consuming page integration, prop values, and redirect behaviour.\n* Depends on SFCC-736 (drawer base component) — this component extends the base drawer shell.\n* Jasmijn: Confirm the exact component name for the current-country display row (Figma instance Frame 2147224873) — separate atom or composed inline?\n* Jasmijn: Confirm full country list and region groupings — Figma shows North America, Europe, Asia/Oceania, Africa, Middle East but Africa and Middle East are collapsed in most frames. Full list to be confirmed before build begins.",
            "to_string": "As a Developer, \nI want a reusable {{global/country-currency-selector}} React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \nso that it can be consumed across storefronts to allow shoppers to select their shipping country, currency, and optionally language.\n\n----\n\nThe component is a right-anchored slide-in drawer. It accepts props to control which optional sections render. It does not own redirect logic — it exposes an {{onConfirm(country, locale)}} callback; the consuming page handles the redirect.\n\nFigma: {{QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs}}, nodes {{3193:72555}} (desktop), {{3193:72676}} (desktop with language), {{3193:73142}} (mobile), {{3193:73415}} (mobile with language). UI kit: {{wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm}}, node {{40000938-5082}}."
          }
        ],
