            "from_string": "*Default State*\n\n# Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when the cart renders, then the item displays: product image, product name, price, colour and size, quantity stepper (– quantity +), Remove link, and Wishlist link. \n\n*Quantity Stepper States*\n\n# Given a line item has a quantity of 1, when the cart item renders, then the – control is disabled and visually greyed out.\n# Given a line item has a quantity greater than 1, when the cart item renders, then both the – and + controls are enabled and interactive.\n# Given a line item has reached the maximum purchase quantity, when the cart item renders, then the + control is disabled and visually greyed out.\n## Max Purchase Quantity: [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|smart-link] \n# Given a line item is in a fully OOS or unavailable state, when the cart item renders, then both the – and + controls are disabled and visually greyed out.\n## Out of Stock / Partially out of Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|smart-link] \n## Unavailable Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|smart-link] \n\n*Error State*\n\n# Given a line item is in an error state, when the cart item renders, then a red inline error message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper. Error states include; Out of Stock, Partially Out of Stock, Unavailable Stock\n## Out of Stock / Partially out of Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|smart-link] - “This item is unavailable” or “An item in your bag has limited availability”\n## Unavailable Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|smart-link] - “This item is unavailable” \n\n*Promotional Price State*\n\n# Given a line item has a promotional price applied, when the cart item renders, then the original price is displayed as \"Was $[price]\" and the promotional price as \"Now $[price]\" replacing the standard price display.\n# Given a line item has a promotional price applied, when the cart item renders, then a discount label is displayed beneath the quantity stepper (e.g. \"20% off applied\").\n\n*Warning State*\n\n# Given a line item is in a warning state, when the cart item renders, then a grey info icon and warning message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper. Example warning states include: Maximum purchase quantity reached.\n## Maximum Purchase Quantity Reached: [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|smart-link] - “Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\"\n\n*Responsive*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart on any device, when the cart item renders in any state, then it displays correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n# Given a Shopper navigates a cart item via keyboard, when they tab through it, then focus moves in a logical order: product image → product name → price → quantity stepper (– then +) → Remove link → Wishlist link.\n# Given the quantity stepper renders on a cart item, when a Shopper navigates via keyboard, then both the – and + controls are focusable and activatable via the Enter key.\n# Given the – or + stepper control is disabled (e.g. minimum quantity, maximum quantity, OOS, unavailable), when read by a screen reader, then the control is announced as disabled so the Shopper understands the action is not currently available.\n# Given the Remove and Wishlist links render on a cart item, when read by a screen reader, then both links are announced with descriptive labels that include the product name (e.g. \"Remove Cloud 91 Small Clutch\", \"Add Cloud 91 Small Clutch to Wishlist\") so the Shopper can distinguish between multiple cart items.\n# Given the Wishlist link is disabled due to a product being unavailable, when read by a screen reader, then the Wishlist link is announced as disabled so the Shopper understands the action is not currently available.\n# Given the product image renders on a cart item, when read by a screen reader, then the image has descriptive alt text including the product name.\n# Given an error message renders beneath the stepper (e.g. OOS, limited stock, unavailable), when it appears, then it is announced immediately via an ARIA live region (role=\"alert\") so the Shopper is informed without having to navigate to it.\n# Given a warning message renders beneath the stepper (e.g. maximum quantity reached), when it appears, then it is announced immediately via an ARIA live region (role=\"status\") so the Shopper is informed without having to navigate to it.\n# Given any text or interactive element renders within the cart item, when checked against WCAG 2.1 AA standards, then all text meets a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 and all interactive elements meet a minimum contrast ratio of 3:1.\n# Given any state is communicated within the cart item (e.g. error message in red, warning message in grey, disabled stepper), when it renders, then the state is not conveyed by colour alone — icons, text labels, or ARIA attributes also communicate the meaning.\n# Given the – and + stepper controls, Remove link, and Wishlist link render on mobile, when a Shopper taps them, then each interactive element meets the minimum touch target size of 44x44px in line with WCAG 2.1 AA",
            "to_string": "*Default State*\n\n# Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when the cart renders, then the item displays: product image, product name, price, colour and size, quantity stepper (– quantity +), Remove link, and Wishlist link. \n\n*Quantity Stepper States*\n\n# Given a line item has a quantity of 1, when the cart item renders, then the – control is disabled and visually greyed out.\n# Given a line item has a quantity greater than 1, when the cart item renders, then both the – and + controls are enabled and interactive.\n# Given a line item has reached the maximum purchase quantity, when the cart item renders, then the + control is disabled and visually greyed out.\n## Max Purchase Quantity: [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|smart-link] \n# Given a line item is in a fully OOS or unavailable state, when the cart item renders, then both the – and + controls are disabled and visually greyed out.\n## Out of Stock / Partially out of Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|smart-link] \n## Unavailable Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|smart-link] \n\n*Error State*\n\n# Given a line item is in an error state, when the cart item renders, then a red inline error message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper. Error states include; Out of Stock, Partially Out of Stock, Unavailable Stock\n## Out of Stock / Partially out of Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-282|smart-link] - “This item is unavailable” or “An item in your bag has limited availability”\n## Unavailable Stock - [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-796|smart-link] - “This item is unavailable” \n\n*Promotional Price State*\n\n# Given a line item has a promotional price applied, when the cart item renders, then the original price is displayed as \"Was $[price]\" and the promotional price as \"Now $[price]\" replacing the standard price display.\n# Given a line item has a promotional price applied, when the cart item renders, then a discount label is displayed beneath the quantity stepper (e.g. \"20% off applied\").\n\n*Warning State*\n\n# Given a line item is in a warning state, when the cart item renders, then a grey info icon and warning message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper. Example warning states include: Maximum purchase quantity reached.\n## Maximum Purchase Quantity Reached: [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-250|smart-link] - “Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\"\n\n*Responsive*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart on any device, when the cart item renders in any state, then it displays correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n# Given a Shopper navigates a cart item via keyboard, when they tab through it, then focus moves in a logical order: product image → product name → price → quantity stepper (– then +) → Remove link → Wishlist link.\n# Given the quantity stepper renders on a cart item, when a Shopper navigates via keyboard, then both the – and + controls are focusable and activatable via the Enter key.\n# Given the – or + stepper control is disabled (e.g. minimum quantity, maximum quantity, OOS, unavailable), when read by a screen reader, then the control is announced as disabled so the Shopper understands the action is not currently available.\n# Given the Remove and Wishlist links render on a cart item, when read by a screen reader, then both links are announced with descriptive labels that include the product name and size (e.g. \"Remove Cloud 91 Small Clutch Size 38\", \"Add Cloud 91 Small Clutch Size 38 to Wishlist\") so the Shopper can distinguish between multiple cart items.\n# Given the Wishlist link is disabled due to a product being unavailable, when read by a screen reader, then the Wishlist link is announced as disabled so the Shopper understands the action is not currently available.\n# Given the product image renders on a cart item, when read by a screen reader, then the image has descriptive alt text including the product name.\n# Given an error message renders beneath the stepper (e.g. OOS, limited stock, unavailable), when it appears, then it is announced immediately via an ARIA live region (role=\"alert\") so the Shopper is informed without having to navigate to it.\n# Given a warning message renders beneath the stepper (e.g. maximum quantity reached), when it appears, then it is announced immediately via an ARIA live region (role=\"status\") so the Shopper is informed without having to navigate to it.\n# Given any text or interactive element renders within the cart item, when checked against WCAG 2.1 AA standards, then all text meets a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 and all interactive elements meet a minimum contrast ratio of 3:1.\n# Given any state is communicated within the cart item (e.g. error message in red, warning message in grey, disabled stepper), when it renders, then the state is not conveyed by colour alone — icons, text labels, or ARIA attributes also communicate the meaning.\n# Given the – and + stepper controls, Remove link, and Wishlist link render on mobile, when a Shopper taps them, then each interactive element meets the minimum touch target size of 44x44px in line with WCAG 2.1 AA",
