            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "# Given a shopper has items in their cart, when the cart page loads on desktop, then each Cart Item tile renders the following elements in order: product image (left), product name, price, colour, size, price, quantity stepper (- quantity +), Remove link, and Wishlist link, consistent with the Figma design.\n# Given a shopper views the cart on mobile, when the cart page loads, then each Cart Item tile renders all elements correctly sized and positioned for the mobile viewport — no detail is truncated or hidden, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n\n\n\n\nNeed to include errors, warnings etc - everything from a UI perspective",
            "to_string": "*Default State*\n\n# Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when the cart renders, then the item displays: product image, product name, price, colour and size, quantity stepper (– quantity +), Remove link, and Wishlist link. \n\nQuantity Stepper States\n\n# Given a line item has a quantity of 1, when the cart item renders, then the – control is disabled and visually greyed out.\n\nError State\n\n# Given a line item has an error (e.g. OOS or limited stock), when the cart item renders, then a red inline error message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper\n\nPromotional Price\n\n# Given a line item has a promotional price applied, when the cart item renders, then the original price is displayed as \"Was $[price]\" and the promotional price as \"Now $[price]\" replacing the standard price display.\n# Given a line item has a promotional price applied, when the cart item renders, then a discount label is displayed beneath the quantity stepper (e.g. \"20% off applied\").\n\nResponsive\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart on any device, when the cart item renders in any state, then it displays correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.\n\nAccessibility\n\nGiven the Remove and Wishlist links render on a cart item, when navigated via keyboard or read by a screen reader, then both links are focusable, activatable via the Enter key, and announced with descriptive labels.\n\nGiven an error or warning message renders beneath the stepper, when read by a screen reader, then the message is announced via an ARIA live region so the Shopper is informed without having to navigate to it.",
