      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "*Structure — Desktop*\n\nAC1: Cart item tile renders all elements\nGiven a shopper has items in their cart, when the cart page loads on desktop, then each Cart Item tile renders the following elements in order: product image (left), product name, colour, size, price, quantity stepper (- quantity +), Remove link, and Wishlist link, consistent with the Figma design.\n\nAC2: Product image dimensions\nGiven a cart item tile renders on desktop, when the product image loads, then it is displayed at the correct dimensions and aspect ratio as per the Figma design, with no distortion or cropping.\n\nAC3: Product name, colour and size display\nGiven a cart item tile renders on desktop, when it displays, then the product name is shown in the correct typography, with colour and size displayed below as secondary information, consistent with the Figma design.\n\nAC4: Price display\nGiven a cart item tile renders on desktop, when it displays, then the product price is shown at the correct position and in the correct typography, consistent with the Figma design.\n\nAC5: Quantity stepper layout\nGiven a cart item tile renders on desktop, when the quantity stepper displays, then the - control, quantity value, and + control are displayed inline in the correct order and spacing, consistent with the Figma design.\n\nAC6: Remove and Wishlist links\nGiven a cart item tile renders on desktop, when it displays, then Remove and Wishlist are displayed as underlined text links below the quantity stepper, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Structure — Tablet*\n\nAC7: Cart item tile renders on tablet\nGiven a shopper views the cart on tablet, when the cart page loads, then each Cart Item tile renders all elements correctly sized and positioned for the tablet viewport, consistent with the Figma design.\n\n*Structure — Mobile*\n\nAC8: Cart item tile renders on mobile\nGiven a shopper views the cart on mobile, when the cart page loads, then each Cart Item tile renders all elements correctly sized and positioned for the mobile viewport — no detail is truncated or hidden, consistent with the Figma design.\n\nAC9: Mobile layout stacking\nGiven a cart item tile renders on mobile, when it displays, then the layout adapts correctly for the smaller viewport — confirm exact mobile layout with Figma (stacked vs inline elements).\n\n*Multiple Items*\n\nAC10: Multiple items render independently\nGiven a shopper has multiple items in their cart, when the cart page loads, then each Cart Item tile renders independently and is individually identifiable, with no overlap or layout breaking regardless of item count.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\nAC11: Cart item accessible to screen readers\nGiven a screen reader user navigates to the cart, when they reach a cart item tile, then the product name, price, colour, size, and quantity are all announced correctly.\n\nAC12: Quantity stepper keyboard operable\nGiven a keyboard-only user is interacting with a cart item tile, when they Tab to the quantity stepper and Remove/Wishlist links, then all interactive elements receive focus in a logical order and are operable without a mouse.",
            "to_string": "# Given a shopper has items in their cart, when the cart page loads on desktop, then each Cart Item tile renders the following elements in order: product image (left), product name, price, colour, size, price, quantity stepper (- quantity +), Remove link, and Wishlist link, consistent with the Figma design.\n# Given a shopper views the cart on mobile, when the cart page loads, then each Cart Item tile renders all elements correctly sized and positioned for the mobile viewport — no detail is truncated or hidden, consistent with the Figma design.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
