      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1.\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and the quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1.\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button remains disabled and visually greyed out and the quantity remains at 1.\n* Given a Shopper increments or decrements the quantity of a line item, when the quantity updates, then the cart drawer item count (e.g. Bag • 3), and the order summary, all update accordingly without a full page reload.",
            "to_string": "1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n2. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n3. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled and the quantity remains at 1.\n4. Given a Shopping increments or decrements the quantity of a line item, when the quantity updates, then the cart drawer count (e.g. Bag 3), and the order summary, all update without requiring a full page load",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
          "name": "Isabel Chaloner",
          "email": "isabel.chaloner@accenture.com",
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e5a0df80fa413e572a441e3890e6a12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FIC-6.png"
        },
        "created": "2026-09-01T03:57:00.313000+00:00"
      },
      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n2. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n3. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled and the quantity remains at 1.\n4. Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per [SFCC-250]), when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled, an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\", and an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see [SFCC-274]).\n5. Given the maximum quantity error is displayed, when it renders, then the Checkout CTA is disabled and greyed out until the Shopper resolves the issue (see [SFCC-275]).\n6. Given a Shopper attempts to set a quantity exceeding available inventory, when the action is taken, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Not enough items available\", an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see [SFCC-274]), and checkout is blocked (see [SFCC-275]) until the Shopper resolves the issue by either reducing the quantity to within available stock, removing the item from the cart, or moving the item to their wishlist.\n7. Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "to_string": "* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1.\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and the quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1.\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button remains disabled and visually greyed out and the quantity remains at 1.\n* Given a Shopper increments or decrements the quantity of a line item, when the quantity updates, then the cart drawer item count (e.g. Bag • 3), and the order summary, all update accordingly without a full page reload.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "display_name": "Emma Kirwan",
          "name": "Emma Kirwan",
          "email": null,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/437c30dd63bbb0ec0a2f7c0d8d556d93?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FEK-4.png"
        },
        "created": "2026-09-01T03:56:47.514000+00:00"
      },
      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "# Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1.\n# Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and the quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1.\n# Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button remains disabled and visually greyed out and the quantity remains at 1.\n# Given a Shopper increments or decrements the quantity of a line item, when the quantity updates, then the cart drawer item count (e.g. Bag • 3), and the order summary, all update accordingly without a full page reload.",
            "to_string": "1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n2. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n3. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled and the quantity remains at 1.\n4. Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per [SFCC-250]), when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled, an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\", and an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see [SFCC-274]).\n5. Given the maximum quantity error is displayed, when it renders, then the Checkout CTA is disabled and greyed out until the Shopper resolves the issue (see [SFCC-275]).\n6. Given a Shopper attempts to set a quantity exceeding available inventory, when the action is taken, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Not enough items available\", an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see [SFCC-274]), and checkout is blocked (see [SFCC-275]) until the Shopper resolves the issue by either reducing the quantity to within available stock, removing the item from the cart, or moving the item to their wishlist.\n7. Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "from_id": "",
