            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "*AC1: Increment quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n\n*AC2: Decrement quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n\n*AC3: Minimum quantity (qty 1)*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled, visually greyed out, and the quantity remains at 1. \n\n*AC4. Maximum quantity — + disabled*\n\n* Given a Shopper reaches the maximum quantity allowed per SKU (as per SFCC-250), when the limit is reached, then the + control becomes disabled and visually greyed out.\n\n*AC4b. Maximum quantity — error message on tap*\n\n* Given the + control is disabled due to the maximum quantity limit and the Shopper taps it, when the tap is registered, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size.\"\n\n*AC5. Inventory limit — + disabled*\n\n* Given a Shopper reaches the maximum available inventory for a variant based on the 15-minute delta feed, when the limit is reached, then the + control becomes disabled and visually greyed out.\n\n*AC5b. Inventory limit — error message on tap*\n\n* Given the + control is disabled due to the inventory limit and the Shopper taps it, when the tap is registered, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Not enough items available.\"\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Additional Scenarios:*{color}\n\n* {color:#ff5630}Inventory drops below the customer’s current cart quantity e.g. Customer has 3 units, delta feed runs, only 2 now available.{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Does the cart automatically refresh when the delta feed updates, or only on page load/manual refresh? While the cart session is open, against the 15 min delta{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}If the quantity is auto-adjusted downward, is this silent or does the customer see a notification?{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Inventory drops to zero while in cart e.g. e.g. Customer has 1 unit in cart, item goes fully OOS between delta feeds.{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Does the line item automatically show the OOS state or does it only update on next page load?{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Inventory increases while in cart e.g. Customer couldn't add more units, delta feed runs, more stock becomes available.{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Does the + re-enable automatically when inventory increases per the delta feed?{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Or does the customer need to refresh the page to see the updated availability?{color}\n\n\n\n*AC6: Order summary recalculation*\n\n** Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "to_string": "*AC1: Increment quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n\n*AC2: Decrement quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n\n*AC3: Minimum quantity (qty 1)*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled, visually greyed out, and the quantity remains at 1. \n\n*AC4. Maximum quantity — + disabled*\n\n* Given a Shopper reaches the maximum quantity allowed per SKU (as per SFCC-250), when the limit is reached, then the + control becomes disabled and visually greyed out.\n\n*AC4b. Maximum quantity — error message on tap*\n\n* Given the + control is disabled due to the maximum quantity limit and the Shopper taps it, when the tap is registered, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size.\"\n\n*AC5. Inventory limit — + disabled*\n\n* Given a Shopper reaches the maximum available inventory for a variant based on the 15-minute delta feed, when the limit is reached, then the + control becomes disabled and visually greyed out.\n\n*AC5b. Inventory limit — error message on tap*\n\n* Given the + control is disabled due to the inventory limit and the Shopper taps it, when the tap is registered, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Not enough items available.\"\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Additional Scenarios:*{color}\n\n* {color:#ff5630}Inventory drops below the customer’s current cart quantity e.g. Customer has 3 units, delta feed runs, only 2 now available.{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Does the cart automatically refresh when the delta feed updates, or only on page load/manual refresh? While the cart session is open, against the 15 min delta{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}If the quantity is auto-adjusted downward, is this silent or does the customer see a notification?{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Inventory drops to zero while in cart e.g. e.g. Customer has 1 unit in cart, item goes fully OOS between delta feeds.{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Does the line item automatically show the OOS state or does it only update on next page load?{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Inventory increases while in cart e.g. Customer couldn't add more units, delta feed runs, more stock becomes available.{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Does the + re-enable automatically when inventory increases per the delta feed?{color}\n** {color:#ff5630}Or does the customer need to refresh the page to see the updated availability?{color}\n\n\n\n*AC6: Order summary recalculation*\n\n** Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.\n\n\n\n*Add an AC around the cart drawer being updated when the quantity of the bag increases.*",
