            "from_string": "*AC1: Increment quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n\n*AC2: Decrement quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n\n*AC3: Minimum quantity (qty 1)*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled, visually greyed out, and the quantity remains at 1. \n\n*AC4: Maximum quantity reached*\n\n* Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per SFCC-250), when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled, an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\", and an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see SFCC-274).\n\n*Checkout blocked at max quantity*\n\n\n\nInventory error\n\n\n\nOrder summary recalculation\n\n\n* Minimum quantity (qty 1)\n* \n* \n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled, visually greyed out, and the quantity remains at 1. \n4. Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per [SFCC-250] , when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled and visually greyed out, an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\", and an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see [SFCC-274] )\n5. Given a Shopper attempts to set a quantity exceeding available inventory, when the action is taken, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Not enough items available\", an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA (see [SFCC-274]), and checkout is blocked (see [SFCC-275]) until the Shopper resolves the issue by either reducing the quantity to within available stock, removing the item from the cart, or moving the item to their wishlist.\n7. Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "to_string": "*AC1: Increment quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n\n*AC2: Decrement quantity*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n\n*AC3: Minimum quantity (qty 1)*\n\n* Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled, visually greyed out, and the quantity remains at 1. \n\n*AC4: Maximum quantity reached*\n\n* Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per [SFCC-250] ), when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled, an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\"\n\n*AC5: Inventory error*\n\n* Given a Shopper attempts to set a quantity exceeding available inventory, when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled and visually greyed out, the quantity is capped at the maximum available stock level, and an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Not enough items available\".\"\n\n*AC6: Order summary recalculation*\n\n** Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
