            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Shopper, I want to increase or decrease the quantity of an item directly from the cart page, so that I can adjust my order without returning to the product page.\n\nThe quantity stepper uses – and + controls. Cart totals must update upon quantity change. Maximum quantity per SKU is governed by CAI-017 (max 3 units). All quantity and inventory data is served from SFCC. Current site behaviour when a customer attempts to exceed available inventory is to display a \"quantity not available / not enough items for sale\" error message and block checkout — this behaviour should be retained unless otherwise confirmed.\n\n*Image for reference (figma leading):*\n\n!image-20260803-234037.png|width=1149,alt=\"image-20260803-234037.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260803-234106.png|width=1149,alt=\"image-20260803-234106.png\"!",
            "to_string": "As a Shopper, I want to increase or decrease the quantity of an item directly from the cart page, so that I can adjust my order without returning to the product page.\n\nThe quantity stepper uses – and + controls. Cart totals must update upon quantity change. Maximum quantity per SKU is governed by CAI-017 (max 3 units). All quantity and inventory data is served from SFCC. \n\n*Image for reference (figma leading):*\n\n!image-20260803-234037.png|width=1149,alt=\"image-20260803-234037.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260803-234106.png|width=1149,alt=\"image-20260803-234106.png\"!"
