            "from_string": "1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n2. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n3. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then an inline error message is displayed (e.g. \"Enter a number greater than 0\") and the quantity remains at 1.\n4. Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per [SFCC-250]), when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled and an inline error message is displayed.\n5. Given a Shopper attempts to set a quantity exceeding available inventory, when the action is taken, then an error message is displayed (e.g. \"Not enough items available\") and checkout is blocked until the Shopper resolves the issue by either reducing the quantity to within available stock, removing the item from the cart, or moving the item to their wishlist.\n6. Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "to_string": "1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap +, then the item quantity increments by 1 and the item total and order summary update accordingly.\n2. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they tap – and quantity is greater than 1, then the quantity decrements by 1 and totals update.\n3. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled and the quantity remains at 1.\n4. Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group (as per SFCC-250), when they tap +, then the + control becomes disabled and an inline error message is displayed.\n5. Given a Shopper attempts to set a quantity exceeding available inventory, when the action is taken, then an error message is displayed (e.g. \"Not enough items available\") and checkout is blocked until the Shopper resolves the issue by either reducing the quantity to within available stock, removing the item from the cart, or moving the item to their wishlist.\n6. Given a quantity change is made, when the update is processed, then the order summary (subtotal, GST, grand total) reflects the updated quantity without a full page reload.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
