            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Developer, I want to build the cart drawer as a reusable PWA Kit component, so that it can be triggered from any surface on the site and render the correct state based on the current basket contents.\n\nAs a Shopper, I want the cart to open as a full-screen overlay that takes over the page, so that I can view and manage my bag with full focus before returning to browsing.\n\nWhen triggered, the cart renders as a full-screen overlay that takes over the entire screen — it is not a partial slide-in panel. The background page content is obscured behind the overlay. The overlay has two header states depending on cart content — when the cart contains items the header displays \"BAG\" with a dynamic item count and an X close icon; when the cart is empty the header displays \"YOUR BAG IS EMPTY\" with an X close icon. This component is the container for all other cart stories and is a dependency for SFCC-270 through SFCC-301.\n\nAll cart state and item count data is served from SFCC via the PWA Kit. The overlay itself is a PWA Kit component — no Contentful involvement in the overlay/header behaviour.\n\nImage for reference (Figma is leading):\n\nFull Cart\n\n\\!image-20260803-235728.png|alt=\"image-20260803-235728.png\"\\!\n\nEmpty Cart\n\n\\!image-20260803-235740.png|alt=\"image-20260803-235740.png\"\\!",
