      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Dependency",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "to_string": "@Design: Open item — confirm whether clicking outside the cart panel on the overlay should close the panel (AC6).\n@Design: Open item — confirm the mobile behaviour — full screen or partial overlay (AC7).\n@Design: Open item — confirm whether \"YOUR BAG IS EMPTY\" in the empty cart header is the same as the Contentful-managed heading in SFCC-277, or whether the header label is hardcoded separately from the empty cart body content.",
            "to_id": ""
          },
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "to_string": "1. Given a Shopper opens the cart, when the panel renders, then it slides in from the right as an overlay drawer without navigating away from the current page.\n2. Given the cart contains items, when the panel header renders, then it displays \"BAG • [item count]\" left aligned with an X close icon right aligned.\n3. Given the cart is empty, when the panel header renders, then it displays \"YOUR BAG IS EMPTY\" left aligned with an X close icon right aligned.\n4. Given a Shopper adds or removes an item, when the cart updates, then the item count in the header updates dynamically to reflect the new total.\n5. Given a Shopper clicks the X close icon, when the action is taken, then the cart panel closes and the Shopper remains on the page they were viewing.\n6. Given a Shopper clicks outside the cart panel on the overlay, when the action is taken, then the cart panel closes — confirm with design whether this is the intended behaviour.\n7. Given a Shopper views the cart on mobile, when the panel renders, then it displays full screen rather than as a partial overlay — confirm with design.",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
