      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "*Standard Cart Interaction*\n\n# Given a Shopper has a SKU in their cart and the quantity equals the configured maximum, when the cart renders, then the + control for that line item is disabled and visually greyed out.\n# {color:#ff5630}Given the + control is disabled due to max quantity and the Shopper taps it, when the tap is registered, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size.\"{color}\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the error state renders, then a page-level error banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached\" (see SFCC-404).\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the error state renders, then an error message is displayed in the order summary reading \"Please correct item quantities to proceed\" (see SFCC-274).\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the button remains enabled — max quantity alone does not block checkout.\n\n*Cart Merge*\n\n\n\nGiven a shopper has a variant in their bag and the quantity already equals the applicable maximum, when the bag is loaded or the quantity stepper is rendered, then the increment (+) control for that line item is disabled.\n2. Given the increment control is disabled due to max quantity, when the page renders, then an inline message is displayed below the quantity stepper informing the shopper they have reached the limit for that size.\n3. Given a shopper manually enters a quantity above the applicable maximum, when they confirm or the field loses focus, then the quantity is reset to the maximum and the inline message is displayed.\n4. Given the max quantity limit is reached, when the shopper views the order summary, then the checkout CTA remains enabled — max quantity alone does not block checkout.\n5. Given a shopper reduces the quantity below the limit, when the quantity updates, then the inline message is dismissed and the increment control is re-enabled.\n6. Given no maximum purchase quantity is configured at any level, when a shopper views their bag, then no restriction is applied and standard quantity behaviour applies.\n\n\n\n*AC5. Combined Quantity Exceeds SKU Limit*\n\n* Given a Guest Shopper has items in their cart and signs in to an account where the combined quantity of the same SKU exceeds the maximum of 3 units, when sign-in completes and the baskets merge, then the following occurs across all components simultaneously:\n** Cart Item - The quantity is automatically capped at 3 - the displayed quantity never exceeds the maximum limit\n** Cart Item - The (+) control on the affected line item becomes disabled and visually greyed out\n** Cart Error Banner - A page-level error banner renders at the top of the cart drawer reading “Maximum purchase quantity reached”\n** An error message displays in the order summary reading “Please correct item quantities to proceed”\n** The checkout CTA is disabled and grey until the shopper resolves the quantity by reducing it within the allowed limit",
            "to_string": "*Standard Cart Interaction*\n\n# Given a Shopper has a variant in their cart and the quantity equals the configured maximum of 3, when the cart renders, then the + control for that line item is disabled and visually greyed out while the – control remains enabled.\n# Given a Shopper has a variant in their cart and the quantity equals the configured maximum of 3, when the cart renders, then an inline warning message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\" with an info icon.\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the cart renders, then a page-level warning banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag has reached maximum quantity\" (see SFCC-404).\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the button remains enabled — maximum quantity alone does not block checkout. Apple Pay and Google Pay express buttons also remain enabled.\n\n*Cart Merge*\n\n# Given a Guest Shopper has items in their cart and signs in to an account where the combined quantity of the same SKU exceeds the maximum limit of 3, when sign-in completes and the baskets merge, then the quantity is automatically capped at 3 — it never displays a quantity exceeding the maximum.\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then the + control on the affected line item is disabled and visually greyed out while the – control remains enabled.\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then an inline warning message is displayed beneath the affected line item reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\" with an info icon.\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then a page-level warning banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag has reached maximum quantity\" (see SFCC-404).\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the button remains enabled — the auto-cap resolves the quantity issue and checkout is not blocked (see SFCC-275).",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
