        "items": [
          {
            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Shopper, I want to be clearly informed when I've reached the maximum purchase quantity for a product in my bag, so that I understand why I can't increase the quantity further.\n\nThe maximum SKU purchase quantity is configured globally in Business Manager and enforced at the variant level (per size/colour). When a shopper attempts to increase the quantity of a line item beyond the applicable limit, then an error message will be displayed within the cart item, as well as the order summary. The checkout CTA will remain disabled, until the issue is resolved.\n\n\n\n_Note:_ as per comments on [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-271|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-271|smart-link]  desired behaviour is not allow the customer to go over the max limit and therefore not block the checkout. An enhancement can be raised if required. ",
            "to_string": "As a Shopper, I want to be clearly informed when I've reached the maximum purchase quantity for a product in my bag, so that I understand why I can't increase the quantity further.\n\nThe maximum SKU purchase quantity is configured globally in Business Manager and enforced at the variant level (per size/colour). When a shopper has reached the maximum allowed SKU limit, the + will be disabled, and error messaging will be displayed to the customer. The checkout should never be blocked."
          }
        ],
