          },
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "1. Given a shopper has a variant in their bag and the quantity already equals the configured maximum for their customer group, when the bag is loaded or the quantity stepper is rendered, then the increment (+) control for that line item is disabled.\n2. Given the increment control is disabled due to max quantity, when the page renders, then an inline message is displayed below the quantity stepper (e.g. \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\").\n3. Given a shopper manually enters a quantity above the configured maximum, when they confirm or the field loses focus, then the quantity is reset to the maximum and the inline message is displayed.\n4. Given the max quantity limit is reached, when the shopper views the order summary, then the checkout CTA remains enabled (max quantity alone does not block checkout).\n5. Given different customer groups have different configured limits, when a shopper belonging to a specific customer group views their bag, then the enforcement reflects the limit configured for their customer group — not a global default.\n6. Given a shopper is a guest (no customer group assigned), when they reach the default maximum quantity, then the default customer group limit is enforced.\n7. Given the max quantity message is displayed, when the shopper reduces the quantity below the limit, then the inline message is dismissed and the increment control is re-enabled.",
            "to_string": "1. Given a shopper has a variant in their bag and the quantity already equals the applicable maximum, when the bag is loaded or the quantity stepper is rendered, then the increment (+) control for that line item is disabled.\n2. Given the increment control is disabled due to max quantity, when the page renders, then an inline message is displayed below the quantity stepper informing the shopper they have reached the limit for that size.\n3. Given a shopper manually enters a quantity above the applicable maximum, when they confirm or the field loses focus, then the quantity is reset to the maximum and the inline message is displayed.\n4. Given the max quantity limit is reached, when the shopper views the order summary, then the checkout CTA remains enabled — max quantity alone does not block checkout.\n5. Given a shopper reduces the quantity below the limit, when the quantity updates, then the inline message is dismissed and the increment control is re-enabled.\n6. Given no maximum purchase quantity is configured at any level, when a shopper views their bag, then no restriction is applied and standard quantity behaviour applies.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
