        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "DOMESTIC ROUTING\n1. Given a Shopper views the cart with items and no errors on a domestic storefront, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is displayed and enabled.\n2. Given a Shopper on a domestic storefront clicks the enabled Checkout button regardless of authentication status, when the action is triggered, then they are taken directly to the SFCC checkout entry page without an intermediate login step.\n\nINTERNATIONAL ROUTING\n3. Given a Shopper views the cart with items and no errors on an international storefront, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is displayed and enabled.\n4. Given a Shopper on an international storefront clicks the enabled Checkout button, when the action is triggered, then they are directed to a sign-in page before being handed off to the Global-e checkout flow (see [SFCC-63])\n\nDISABLE / ENABLE STATES (DOMESTIC AND INTERNATIONAL)\n5. Given a line item in the cart has a quantity or inventory error, when the error is present, then the Checkout button is disabled and greyed out (see [SFCC-271] ACs 4, 5, and 6).\n6. Given a fully out-of-stock item is present in the cart, when the error is present, then the Checkout button is disabled and greyed out (see [SFCC-282]).\n7. Given the cart is empty, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is not visible (see [SFCC-277]).\n8. Given a Shopper resolves all errors in the cart, when the last error is resolved, then the Checkout button returns to its enabled state.\n\nRESPONSIVE\n11. Given a Shopper is on any device, when they view the cart, then the Checkout button renders and functions correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.",
            "to_string": "# Given the cart contains one or more items with no errors, when the cart summary component renders, then the button group displays in the following order: Checkout CTA (primary, full-width black button), Apple Pay Express button (outlined), Google Pay Express button (outlined).\n# Given the cart contains an error condition (fully OOS, partially OOS, unavailable item, or quantity error requiring customer action), when the error state renders, then the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay Express button, and Google Pay Express button are all disabled and visually greyed out simultaneously.\n# Given a Shopper resolves all error conditions in the cart, when the last error is resolved, then the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay Express button, and Google Pay Express button all re-enable simultaneously.\n# Given a Shopper clicks the enabled Checkout CTA regardless of authentication status or storefront, when the action is triggered, then they are directed to the SFCC checkout page. _For international storefronts, the checkout experience is the same but Global-e renders within an iframe at the appropriate step (see SFCC-63)._\n# Given a Shopper views the button group on any device, when it renders, then all buttons display correctly and are fully interactive across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
