            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Shopper, I want a clear and prominent Checkout button on the cart page, so that I can proceed to payment when I am ready.\n\nThis story covers the Checkout CTA only — a full-width black button labelled \"CHECKOUT\" displayed in the order summary panel on both desktop and mobile. The Checkout CTA routing is handled by SFCC and the PWA Kit.\n\nNote: Google Pay Express and Apple Pay Express buttons also appear on the cart page per the Figma designs. These are out of scope for this story — the full button rendering, display logic, browser/device detection, payment flows, and order placement for both are covered in the Payments epic (SFCC-309).\n\n*Image for reference (Figma is leading):*\n\n!image-20260803-235029.png|width=1149,alt=\"image-20260803-235029.png\"!\n\n!image-20260803-235041.png|width=1149,alt=\"image-20260803-235041.png\"!",
            "to_string": "*As a* Shopper, I want to see a clear group of checkout actions in my cart, so that I can proceed to checkout using my preferred payment method.\n\nThis is a *PWA Kit UI component story* covering the button group within the cart summary component (SFCC-816). The button group consists of three buttons rendered in a fixed stacked order: Checkout CTA (primary), Apple Pay Express (secondary), and Google Pay Express (secondary).\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Checkout CTA*{color}{color:#ff5630} — the primary checkout action. All storefronts direct to the same SFCC checkout entry page. For international storefronts, the checkout experience is the same but Global-e renders within an iframe at the appropriate step — the routing and Global-e iframe integration is covered in {color}[https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-63|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-63|smart-link]\n\n*Apple Pay Express* — express checkout via Apple Pay. The Apple Pay integration, browser detection, and show/hide logic based on device/browser eligibility are covered in the Payments epic (SFCC-383) — not this story.\n\n*Google Pay Express* — express checkout via Google Pay. The Google Pay integration, browser detection, and show/hide logic based on device/browser eligibility are covered in the Payments epic (SFCC-384) — not this story.\n\n*Image for reference (Figma is leading):*\n\n!image-20260827-001747.png|width=781,alt=\"image-20260827-001747.png\"!"
          }
        ],
