            "to_string": "1. Given a Shopper views the cart with items and no errors, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is displayed and enabled.\n2. Given a Shopper on a domestic storefront clicks the enabled Checkout button, when the action is triggered, then they are navigated to the SFCC checkout page.\n3. Given a Shopper on an international storefront clicks the enabled Checkout button, when the action is triggered, then they are handed off to the Global-e checkout flow (see [SFCC-63]).\n4. Given a Shopper clicks the Checkout button regardless of authentication status, when the action is triggered, then they are taken directly to the SFCC checkout entry page without an intermediate login step. Open item: confirm with Zimmermann whether this matches intended behaviour for SFCC - on Magento international users are taken to a separate login page first.\n5. Given a line item in the cart has a quantity or inventory error, when the error is present, then the Checkout button is disabled and greyed out (see [SFCC-271] ACs 4, 5, and 6).\n6. Given a fully out-of-stock item is present in the cart, when the error is present, then the Checkout button is disabled and greyed out (see [SFCC-282]).\n7. Given the cart is empty, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is hidden (see [SFCC-277]).\n8. Given a 100% discount promotion is applied and the cart total is zero, when the page renders, then the Checkout button remains enabled and the Shopper can proceed to checkout. Open item: confirm expected behaviour with Zimmermann.\n9. Given a Shopper resolves all errors in the cart, when the last error is resolved, then the Checkout button returns to its enabled state.\n10. Given a Shopper clicks the Checkout button, when the routing decision is being processed, then a loading state is displayed to prevent double-submission.\n11. Given a Shopper is on any device, when they view the cart, then the Checkout button renders and functions correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
