            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Shopper, I want a clear and prominent Checkout button on the cart page as well as the option to pay quickly via Google Pay or Apple Pay, so that I can proceed to payment in the way that suits me.\n\n_Scope of this story: display and rendering only._ This story covers the presence, layout, and display logic of the Checkout CTA, G Pay, and Apple Pay buttons on the cart page. All payment integration logic, payment flows, tokenisation, and order placement behaviour for G Pay and Apple Pay are out of scope here and covered entirely in the Payments epic. This story is complete when the buttons are correctly displayed and the Checkout CTA navigates to the checkout entry page — payment flow testing requires the Payments epic to be in place.\n\nThe Checkout CTA is a full-width black button labelled \"CHECKOUT\". Below it sit G Pay and Apple Pay buttons, visible on both desktop and mobile.\n\n*Image for reference (Figma is leading):*\n\n!image-20260803-064937.png|width=1134,alt=\"image-20260803-064937.png\"!",
            "to_string": "As a Shopper, I want a clear and prominent Checkout button on the cart page, so that I can proceed to payment when I am ready.\n\nThis story covers the Checkout CTA only — a full-width black button labelled \"CHECKOUT\" displayed in the order summary panel on both desktop and mobile. The Checkout CTA routing is handled by SFCC and the PWA Kit.\n\nNote: Google Pay Express and Apple Pay Express buttons also appear on the cart page per the Figma designs. These are out of scope for this story — the full button rendering, display logic, browser/device detection, payment flows, and order placement for both are covered in the Payments epic (SFCC-309).\n\nImage for reference (Figma is leading):"
          },
