            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "1. Given a Shopper views the cart with items, when the page renders, then a full-width black \"CHECKOUT\" button is displayed prominently in the order summary panel.\n2. Given a Shopper clicks the Checkout button, when the action is triggered, then they are navigated to the checkout entry page.\n3. Given a Shopper views the cart on mobile, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is full-width and positioned below the order summary.\n4. Given a Shopper views the cart on a device and browser that supports Google Pay, when the page renders, then a G Pay button is displayed below the Checkout CTA.\n5. Given a Shopper views the cart on a device and browser that supports Apple Pay, when the page renders, then an Apple Pay button is displayed below the Checkout CTA.\n6. Given a Shopper taps the G Pay button, when the action is triggered, then the Google Pay payment flow is initiated — full behaviour defined in the Payments epic.\n7. Given a Shopper taps the Apple Pay button, when the action is triggered, then the Apple Pay payment flow is initiated — full behaviour defined in the Payments epic.\n8. Given a Shopper's device or browser does not support G Pay or Apple Pay, when the page renders, then the unsupported button is not displayed and the Checkout CTA remains visible and functional.",
