            "from_string": "As a Shopper, I want a clear and prominent Checkout button on the cart page as well as the option to pay quickly via Google Pay or Apple Pay, so that I can proceed to payment in the way that suits me.\n\nThe Checkout CTA is a full-width black button labelled \"CHECKOUT\". Below it sit G Pay and Apple Pay buttons, visible on both desktop and mobile. The Checkout CTA routing is handled by SFCC and the PWA Kit. The G Pay and Apple Pay integrations are owned by the Payments epic — this story covers their presence and rendering on the cart page only. Full payment behaviour for both is a dependency on the Payments epic.",
            "to_string": "As a Shopper, I want a clear and prominent Checkout button on the cart page as well as the option to pay quickly via Google Pay or Apple Pay, so that I can proceed to payment in the way that suits me.\n\nThe Checkout CTA is a full-width black button labelled \"CHECKOUT\". Below it sit G Pay and Apple Pay buttons, visible on both desktop and mobile. The Checkout CTA routing is handled by SFCC and the PWA Kit. The G Pay and Apple Pay integrations are owned by the Payments epic - this story covers their presence and rendering on the cart page only. Full payment behaviour for both is a dependency on the Payments epic.\n\n*Image for reference (figma leading):*\n\n!image-20260803-004420.png|width=875,alt=\"image-20260803-004420.png\"!"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
          "name": "Isabel Chaloner",
          "email": "isabel.chaloner@accenture.com",
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e5a0df80fa413e572a441e3890e6a12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FIC-6.png"
        },
        "created": "2026-08-03T00:44:32.118000+00:00"
      },
      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Attachment",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "to_string": "image-20260803-004420.png",
            "to_id": "12162"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "display_name": "Isabel Chaloner",
          "name": "Isabel Chaloner",
          "email": "isabel.chaloner@accenture.com",
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e5a0df80fa413e572a441e3890e6a12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FIC-6.png"
        },
        "created": "2026-08-03T00:44:32.413000+00:00"
      },
      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Dependency",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "to_string": "@Jasmijn Tsang / @Zimmermann: Open item — the decision on whether a real-time inventory check fires between cart and checkout entry is still pending with Zimmermann. Once confirmed, the behaviour of the Checkout CTA when a stock check fails (disabled state, error messaging) will need to be added to this story or covered in the inventory check story.\n@Payments epic: G Pay and Apple Pay integration behaviour (payment sheet, tokenisation, order placement) must be fully defined and implemented in the Payments epic before ACs 6 and 7 can be tested end-to-end.",
            "to_id": ""
          },
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "to_string": "1. Given a Shopper views the cart with items, when the page renders, then a full-width black \"CHECKOUT\" button is displayed prominently in the order summary panel.\n2. Given a Shopper clicks the Checkout button, when the action is triggered, then they are navigated to the checkout entry page.\n3. Given a Shopper views the cart on mobile, when the page renders, then the Checkout button is full-width and positioned below the order summary.\n4. Given a Shopper views the cart on a device and browser that supports Google Pay, when the page renders, then a G Pay button is displayed below the Checkout CTA.\n5. Given a Shopper views the cart on a device and browser that supports Apple Pay, when the page renders, then an Apple Pay button is displayed below the Checkout CTA.\n6. Given a Shopper taps the G Pay button, when the action is triggered, then the Google Pay payment flow is initiated — full behaviour defined in the Payments epic.\n7. Given a Shopper taps the Apple Pay button, when the action is triggered, then the Apple Pay payment flow is initiated — full behaviour defined in the Payments epic.\n8. Given a Shopper's device or browser does not support G Pay or Apple Pay, when the page renders, then the unsupported button is not displayed and the Checkout CTA remains visible and functional.",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
