          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "*drawer/filters variants*\n\n# Given the drawer renders with Tab=Filters, when it opens, then the drawer/filters component displays the configured filter facet groups as accordions.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (All), when the accordion is expanded, then all top-level category options are displayed as radio buttons per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (Dresses), when the accordion is expanded, then Dresses sub-category options (Mini, Midi, Maxi, Wrap, Evening, Day Dresses, Coverups) are displayed as radio buttons per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Selected, when a filter value has been chosen, then the selected value renders as a chip/tag inside the expanded accordion, replacing the options list.\n\n*Accordion*\n\n# Given the drawer renders, when it loads, then only one accordion can be expanded at a time — expanding a new accordion collapses the previously expanded one.\n# Given an accordion has variant=Expanded, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is open and its content is visible.\n# Given an accordion has variant=Collapsed, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is closed and only the label is visible.\n# Given a shopper clicks an accordion header, when the action occurs, then the accordion toggles between expanded and collapsed states.\n\n*Facet content*\n\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Colour, when the accordion is expanded, then colour options render as a stacked checkbox-group with colour swatches per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Size, when the accordion is expanded, then three sub-groups render: Clothing (0P–4), Accessories (S, M, L, One Size), and Shoes (36–41), each with their respective button styles.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Availability, when the accordion is expanded, then two checkbox options render: Available and Coming Soon.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Material, when the accordion is expanded, then material options render as a stacked checkbox-group per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Sleeve Length, when the accordion is expanded, then sleeve length options render as a stacked checkbox-group per the Figma spec.\n\n*CLEAR and APPLY*\n\n# Given the drawer renders, when it loads, then the CLEAR button (Secondary) and APPLY button (Primary) are displayed side by side at the bottom of the drawer via the Button-group component with layout=Inline.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n# Given the component renders, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.\n# Given each accordion renders, when a screen reader encounters the accordion header, then it is announced with its label and expanded/collapsed state.\n# Given a keyboard user navigates the drawer, when they tab through it, then all accordions, filter options, CLEAR, and APPLY are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\n# Given the CLEAR button renders, when a screen reader encounters it, then it is announced with a label that conveys its purpose.",
            "to_string": "*drawer/filters variants*\n\n# Given the drawer renders with Tab=Filters, when it opens, then the drawer/filters component displays the configured filter facet groups as accordions.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (All), when the accordion is expanded, then all top-level category options are displayed as radio buttons per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (Dresses), when the accordion is expanded, then Dresses sub-category options are displayed as radio buttons per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Selected, when a filter value has been chosen, then the selected value renders as a chip/tag inside the expanded accordion, replacing the options list.\n\n*Accordion*\n\n# Given the drawer renders, when it loads, then only one accordion can be expanded at a time — expanding a new accordion collapses the previously expanded one.\n# Given an accordion has variant=Expanded, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is open and its content is visible.\n# Given an accordion has variant=Collapsed, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is closed and only the label is visible.\n# Given a shopper clicks an accordion header, when the action occurs, then the accordion toggles between expanded and collapsed states.\n\n*Facet content*\n\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Colour, when the accordion is expanded, then colour options render as a stacked checkbox-group with colour swatches per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Size, when the accordion is expanded, then three sub-groups render: Clothing (0P–4), Accessories (S, M, L, One Size), and Shoes (36–41), each with their respective button styles.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Availability, when the accordion is expanded, then two checkbox options render: Available and Coming Soon.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Material, when the accordion is expanded, then material options render as a stacked checkbox-group per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Sleeve Length, when the accordion is expanded, then sleeve length options render as a stacked checkbox-group per the Figma spec.\n\n*CLEAR and APPLY*\n\n# Given the drawer renders, when it loads, then the CLEAR button (Secondary) and APPLY button (Primary) are displayed side by side at the bottom of the drawer via the Button-group component with layout=Inline.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n# Given the component renders, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.\n# Given each accordion renders, when a screen reader encounters the accordion header, then it is announced with its label and expanded/collapsed state.\n# Given a keyboard user navigates the drawer, when they tab through it, then all accordions, filter options, CLEAR, and APPLY are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\n# Given the CLEAR button renders, when a screen reader encounters it, then it is announced with a label that conveys its purpose.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
