        "items": [
          {
            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "drawer/filters variants\n\n# Given the drawer renders with Tab=Filters, when it opens, then the drawer/filters component is displayed showing the configured filter facet groups as accordions.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (All), when the accordion is expanded, then all category options are displayed as per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (Dresses), when the accordion is expanded, then sub-category options for Dresses are displayed as per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Selected, when the component renders, then currently selected filter values are displayed.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Colour, Size, Availability, Material, or Sleeve Length, when the accordion is expanded, then the corresponding filter facet content area renders ready to receive facet content from SFCC-108.\n\nAccordion\n\n# Given an accordion has variant=Expanded, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is open and its content is visible.\n# Given an accordion has variant=Collapsed, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is closed and only the label is visible.\n# Given a shopper clicks an accordion header, when the action occurs, then the accordion toggles between expanded and collapsed states.\n\nCLEAR and APPLY\n\n# Given the drawer is open with filters visible, when the shopper clicks CLEAR, then all selected filter values are cleared and the accordion selections reset.\n# Given the shopper has selected one or more filter values, when they click APPLY, then the drawer closes and the product grid updates to reflect the applied filters.\n# Given the drawer renders, when it loads, then the CLEAR button (Secondary) and APPLY button (Primary) are displayed side by side at the bottom of the drawer via the Button-group component.\n\nAccessibility\n\n# Given the component renders, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.\n# Given each accordion renders, when a screen reader encounters the accordion header, then it is announced with its label and expanded/collapsed state.\n# Given a keyboard user navigates the drawer, when they tab through it, then all accordions, filter options, CLEAR, and APPLY are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\n# Given the CLEAR button renders, when a screen reader encounters it, then it is announced with a label that conveys its purpose.",
            "to_string": "drawer/filters variants\n\n# Given the drawer renders with Tab=Filters, when it opens, then the drawer/filters component is displayed showing the configured filter facet groups as accordions.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (All), when the accordion is expanded, then all category options are displayed as per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Category - PLP (Dresses), when the accordion is expanded, then sub-category options for Dresses are displayed as per the Figma spec.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Selected, when the component renders, then currently selected filter values are displayed.\n# Given drawer/filters variant=Colour, Size, Availability, Material, or Sleeve Length, when the accordion is expanded, then the corresponding filter facet content area renders ready to receive facet content from [SFCC-108].\n\nAccordion\n\n# Given an accordion has variant=Expanded, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is open and its content is visible.\n# Given an accordion has variant=Collapsed, when the drawer renders, then the facet group is closed and only the label is visible.\n# Given a shopper clicks an accordion header, when the action occurs, then the accordion toggles between expanded and collapsed states.\n\nCLEAR and APPLY\n\n# Given the drawer is open with filters visible, when the shopper clicks CLEAR, then all selected filter values are cleared and the accordion selections reset.\n# Given the shopper has selected one or more filter values, when they click APPLY, then the drawer closes and the product grid updates to reflect the applied filters.\n# Given the drawer renders, when it loads, then the CLEAR button (Secondary) and APPLY button (Primary) are displayed side by side at the bottom of the drawer via the Button-group component.\n\nAccessibility\n\n# Given the component renders, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.\n# Given each accordion renders, when a screen reader encounters the accordion header, then it is announced with its label and expanded/collapsed state.\n# Given a keyboard user navigates the drawer, when they tab through it, then all accordions, filter options, CLEAR, and APPLY are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\n# Given the CLEAR button renders, when a screen reader encounters it, then it is announced with a label that conveys its purpose.",
