            "from_string": "*Core component*\n\n# Given a product is passed to the card component, when it renders, then the primary product image and product name are always displayed regardless of variation.\n# Given a product has a badge (e.g. Runway), when the card renders in any variation, then the badge is displayed in the correct position per Figma.\n# Given the component is built as a PWA component, when imported into any page surface, then it renders correctly without page-specific logic embedded in the component itself.\n# Given the card renders, when on desktop and the user hovers{color:#ff5630}, {color}then the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.\n\n*PLP variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, badge, price (incl. was/now), and cart icon are visible.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible and the price disappears.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on mobile, then the size selector is not displayed.\n# Given a product is out of stock, when the card renders, then the cart is greyed out and a notify me link appears.\n\n*Home page variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on home page, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, and badge are displayed.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the price (incl. was/now) appears.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on mobile, then the user only sees the image and name.\n\n*Wishlist variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on the wishlist, when it is in the default state, then the cart icon, name, colour, size, badge, and price (incl. was/now) are displayed.\n# Given the card renders on the wishlist, then there is an close ('x') cta on the top right.\n\n*Variation extensibility*\n\n# Given a new style is introduced in future (e.g. Search), when added to the component, then it can be configured without restructuring the base component.",
            "to_string": "*Core component*\n\n# Given a product is passed to the card component, when it renders, then the primary product image and product name are always displayed regardless of variation.\n# Given a product has a badge (e.g. Runway), when the card renders in any variation, then the badge is displayed in the correct position per Figma.\n# Given the component is built as a PWA component, when imported into any page surface, then it renders correctly without page-specific logic embedded in the component itself.\n# Given the card renders, when on desktop and the user hovers{color:#ff5630}, {color}then the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.\n\n*PLP variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, badge, price (incl. was/now), and cart icon are visible.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible and the price disappears.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on mobile, then the size selector is not displayed.\n# Given a product is out of stock, when the card renders, then the cart is greyed out and a notify me link appears on hover instead of price.\n\n*Home page variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on home page, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, and badge are displayed.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the price (incl. was/now) appears.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on mobile, then the user only sees the image and name.\n\n*Wishlist variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on the wishlist, when it is in the default state, then the image, cart icon, name, colour, size, badge, and price (incl. was/now) are displayed.\n# Given the card renders on the wishlist, then there is a remove ('x') cta on the top right.\n\n*Recently Viewed Full History variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on the full history of recently viewed, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, badge, price (incl. was/now) are displayed.\n\n*Variation extensibility*\n\n# Given a new style is introduced in future (e.g. Search), when added to the component, then it can be configured without restructuring the base component.",
            "from_id": "",
            "to_id": ""
          }
        ],
