            "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
            "fieldtype": "custom",
            "from_string": "1. Given a product is passed to the card component, when it renders, then the primary product image, product name, and price are displayed.\n2. Given a product has a badge (e.g. \"New\", \"Sale\"), when the card renders, then the badge is displayed in the correct position per Figma.\n3. Given a user is on desktop, when they hover over a product card, then the size selector becomes visible.\n4. Given a user is on mobile, when the card renders, then the size selector is not displayed.\n5. Given a product card renders on any surface, then the wishlist icon is present and tappable.\n6. Given a product is out of stock, when the card renders, then the out-of-stock state is displayed correctly per Figma design.\n7. Given the component is built as a PWA component, when imported into another page (PLP, search results, etc.), then it renders correctly without page-specific logic embedded.",
            "to_string": "Core component\n1. Given a product is passed to the card component with any valid style prop, when it renders, then the primary product image and product name are always displayed regardless of variation.\n2. Given a product has a badge (e.g. New, Sale), when the card renders in any variation, then the badge is displayed in the correct position per Figma.\n3. Given a product is out of stock, when the card renders in any variation, then the out-of-stock state is displayed correctly per Figma design.\n4. Given the component is built as a PWA component, when imported into any page surface, then it renders correctly without page-specific logic embedded in the component itself.\n\nPLP variation (style=plp)\n5. Given the card renders with style=plp, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible.\n6. Given the card renders with style=plp, when on mobile, then the size selector is not displayed.\n7. Given the card renders with style=plp, then price and wishlist icon are displayed.\n\nHomepage variation (style=homepage)\n8. Given the card renders with style=homepage, then price, wishlist icon, and size selector are not displayed.\n\nVariation extensibility\n9. Given a new style prop value is introduced in future (e.g. style=search), when added to the component, then it can be configured without restructuring the base component.",
