            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Shopper, I want each product card to display consistent visual information (image, name, price, badge, wishlist icon, size selector, and stock state) as a reusable component, so that the same tile can be used across PLP, PDP, and any other surface that needs to present a product.\n\nThis story covers the build of the shared Product Card / Tile component as a standalone, reusable PWA component. It is split from SFCC-80 (PLP UI – Product Grid & Tile Component) per architect direction. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. The PLP grid layout and \"View More\" pagination remain in SFCC-80. This component will be consumed by SFCC-80 once built.",
            "to_string": "As a Shopper, I want product cards to display relevant information for the surface I am browsing, so that each page feels appropriately tailored without inconsistent component implementations across the site.\n\nThis story covers the build of a single shared Product Card PWA component that supports multiple display variations via a style prop. Each variation controls which elements are shown — the component itself is built and maintained once. It is split from SFCC-80 per architect direction. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. The PLP grid layout and View More pagination remain in SFCC-80.\n\nVariations in scope: PLP (style=plp): image, name, price, badge, wishlist icon, size selector (desktop hover only), out-of-stock state. Homepage (style=homepage): image, name, badge, out-of-stock state only — no price, no wishlist icon, no size selector. Additional variations follow the same pattern and can be added without a new story."
          }
        ],
