      {
        "items": [
          {
            "field": "description",
            "fieldtype": "jira",
            "from_string": "As a Developer, I want a reusable global/country-language-mismatch React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can be consumed across storefronts to surface country and language mismatch prompts to shoppers in a consistent drawer pattern.\\n\\nThe component covers two variants, both rendered as a right-anchored drawer panel using the shared drawer shell:\\n- Location Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's IP-detected country does not match the current storefront (consumed by SFCC-823)\\n- Language Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's browser language does not match the current EU storefront locale (consumed by SFCC-689)\\n\\nThe component does not own the trigger logic or redirect behaviour — that is handled by the consuming stories. It exposes callbacks for each CTA action and accepts props to control which variant renders.",
            "to_string": "As a Developer, \n\nI want a reusable global/country-language-mismatch React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \n\nso that it can be consumed across storefronts to surface country and language mismatch prompts to shoppers in a consistent drawer pattern.\n\n----\n\nThe component covers two variants, both rendered as a right-anchored drawer panel using the shared drawer shell:\n\nLocation Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's IP-detected country does not match the current storefront (consumed by [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-823|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-823|smart-link] )\n\nLanguage Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's browser language does not match the current EU storefront locale (consumed by [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-689|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-689|smart-link])\n\nThe component does not own the trigger logic or redirect behaviour — that is handled by the consuming stories. It exposes callbacks for each CTA action and accepts props to control which variant renders."
          }
        ],
