      "description": "As a Developer, \nI want a reusable \nproduct-card-group-with-lookbook\n React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \nso that it can render an editorial lookbook layout across pages including Shop the Edit, PDP, PLP and any other pages requiring an editorial lookbook layout.\nThe component renders an optional section header (title + link), an editorial/product-shot image on the left (lookbook slot), and a configurable number of product card slots. The width ratio of the lookbook image to the product tile column is controlled by \ngrid\n; the number of product tiles is controlled by \nqty\n. At \nqty=5\n, four product tiles render in a 2×2 grid alongside the lookbook image or product. It does not own the product data or image source — these are passed as props. \nProps in scope:\nProp\nValues\nNotes\nsize\nDesktop, Tablet, Mobile\nControls layout breakpoint\ngrid\n3, 4\nControls width ratio of lookbook image to product tile column. Grid 3 = 2/3 image width; Grid 4 = 3/4 image width. Desktop only — no visible difference at tablet/mobile.\nqty\n2, 3, 5\nNumber of product tiles to render. qty=2: 1 lookbook image + 1 product tile. qty=3: 1 lookbook image + 2 product tiles stacked vertically. qty=5: 1 lookbook image + 4 product tiles in a 2×2 grid.\nshowTitleAndLink\ntrue, false\nToggles the entire section header\ncardType\nProduct, Editorial",
